A :DEFAULT inside a procedure defined in an SSL data source.
no_default_statements_in_datasource flags it: the catalog says the rule
"Flags every :DEFAULT keyword token in the file". Procedure signatures in
a data source cannot take inline defaults either (they are ordinary
signatures, per diag.datasource_default_required), so as recorded a
procedure inside a data source has no unflagged way to default a
parameter.
A nested procedure defaults its parameters inline instead (`:PARAMETERS nWidth := 4;`),
which neither rule flags (diag.no_default_statements_in_datasource, issue #328).
-- input.ds --
:PARAMETERS sAisle := "A";
:PROCEDURE Pad;
:PARAMETERS sText, nWidth;
:DEFAULT nWidth, 4;
:RETURN Right(Replicate("0", nWidth) + sText, nWidth);
:ENDPROC;
:RETURN DoProc("Pad", {sAisle});
-- format --
:PARAMETERS sAisle := "A";

:PROCEDURE Pad;
	:PARAMETERS sText, nWidth;
	:DEFAULT nWidth, 4;

	:RETURN Right(Replicate("0", nWidth) + sText, nWidth);
:ENDPROC;

:RETURN DoProc("Pad", {sAisle});
-- diagnostics --
4:1-4:9 error no_default_statements_in_datasource: Data source files use inline ':=' defaults in ':PARAMETERS', not separate ':DEFAULT' statements
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
4:1-4:9 error no_default_statements_in_datasource: Data source files use inline ':=' defaults in ':PARAMETERS', not separate ':DEFAULT' statements
